<title>FRANCE: Lagardere suspended limit down.</title>
<headline>Lagardere suspended limit down.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Lagardere failed to requote at 1315 GMT and were suspended limit down, the SBF French stockmarkets authority said.</p>
<p>The stock was suspended at the open on news the government was halting its plans to privatise Thomson SA.</p>
<p>SBF said Lagardere would attempt a requote at 1330 GMT. The new lower limit will be 133.40 francs and the new upper limit will be 147.40 francs, SBF said.</p>
<p>Lagardere had been chosen by the government to take over Thomson, but France's privatisation commission did not back the government's preference. It said it could not agree with Lagardere's plans to sell Thomson Multimedia to Daewoo Electronics.</p>
</text>
